From f919888b059d7fb77a73144ca1e5e08bda600d02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evan Almloff <evanalmloff@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] Adapt tests/wasm companion JS to ESM for wry-bindgen

wry-bindgen loads `module` snippets as native ES modules, so the upstream
CommonJS companions are rewritten in place:
  - `require('wasm-bindgen-test')` -> a lazy Proxy over `window` (Rust exports)
  - `require('assert')`            -> a lazy callable Proxy over `globalThis.__wbgAssert`
  - `exports.NAME = ...`           -> `export const NAME = ...` (or `export { NAME }`)
The `__wbgAssert` global is provided by the test crate. Only the companions whose
Rust files currently pass against wry-bindgen are converted.
